@startuml IJCSA_Theory

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 2
skinparam roundcorner 5
skinparam maxMessageSize 300
skinparam participantPadding 100
skinparam wrapWidth 0
skinparam maxMessageSize 500

participant "Master/\nOrchestrator" as Master
participant "SU₁" as SU1
participant "SU₂" as SU2

== IJCSA: Solve Algebraic Loop at time t ==

Master -> Master: Initialize U^(0) from current inputs

loop until convergence

    note over Master: **1. Evaluate subsystems in parallel**
    
    par Parallel Execution
        Master -> SU1: evaluate_outputs(U1^(m),t)
        activate SU1
        SU1 -> SU1: Y1^(m+1) = S1(U1^(m))
        note right: Compute with dt=0\n(frozen state)
        SU1 --> Master: Y1^(m+1)
        deactivate SU1
    else
        Master -> SU2: evaluate_outputs(U2^(m),t)
        activate SU2
        SU2 -> SU2: Y2^(m+1) = S2(U2^(m))
        note right: Compute with dt=0
        SU2 --> Master: Y2^(m+1)
        deactivate SU2
    end
    
    note over Master: **2. Compute residual**
    
    Master -> Master: r^(m)=[U1^(m)-Y2^(m+1)]\n             [U2^(m)-Y1^(m+1)]
    
    note over Master: **3. Check convergence**
    
    alt ||r^(m)|| < tolerance
        note over Master: ✓ Converged
        Master -> Master: Exit iteration
    end
    
    note over Master: **4. Compute interface Jacobian**
    
    Master -> Master: J^(m) = dR/dU via finite differences
    note right
      For each interface input:
      perturb U_j, evaluate outputs,
      compute J[:, j] = (R_pert - R) / eps
    end note
    
    note over Master: **5. Solve for correction**
    
    Master -> Master: J^(m) · ΔU^(m) = -r^(m)
    
    note over Master: **6. Apply correction**
    
    Master -> Master: U^(m+1)=U^(m)+ΔU^(m)

end

note over Master: **7. Commit converged solution**

Master -> SU1: set_inputs(U1*, t)
activate SU1
SU1 --> Master: inputs committed
deactivate SU1

Master -> SU2: set_inputs(U2*, t)
activate SU2
SU2 --> Master: inputs committed
deactivate SU2

' note over Master, SU2
' **IJCSA Properties:**
' • Interface-level Newton iteration
' • Frozen states (dt=0) during iteration
' • Jacobian via finite differences or directional derivatives
' • Handles algebraic loops through implicit coupling
' • Converges when ||r|| < tolerance
' end note

@enduml